<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Le Moyne d&apos;Iberville, now 44, returns for his pre-travel vaccines. The squadron is expected to sail early next year for the French Antilles and French Guiana, with weeks ashore near Cayenne and Kourou and possible river work inland, and he expects to be away for many months. He has had no fever since his malaria treatment four months ago. The PCR drawn at his last malaria review was negative. The forearm abscess healed within ten days; the culture grew methicillin-susceptible Staphylococcus aureus, and he needed no antibiotic. His screening tests from the preventive visit were negative for HIV and hepatitis C, and the hepatitis B panel shows he is not immune and has never been infected. He has no egg or gelatin allergy, no thymus disease, no immune-suppressing illness or treatment, and has never had yellow fever vaccine. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Destination</td><td>French Antilles and French Guiana, many months, partly inland</td></tr><tr><td>Departure</td><td>Early next year</td></tr><tr><td>Malaria</td><td>No fever in four months</td></tr><tr><td>Screening</td><td>HIV and hepatitis C negative; not immune to hepatitis B</td></tr><tr><td>Vaccine screening</td><td>No contraindication to yellow fever vaccine</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

